# Cursor Rules for vellum (AIRAM SDD)

# 1. Spec-Driven Development
- Always read docs before generating code:
  - Backlog tasks: `docs/05-backlog/02-epics-and-tasks.md`
  - Requirements & Acceptance Criteria: `docs/02-prd/01-product-requirements.md`
  - Architecture & Tech Stack: `docs/03-tech-stack/01-architecture-overview.md`
  - ADRs: `docs/03-tech-stack/adr/`
- Every feature must strictly fulfill the Acceptance Criteria in the PRD.
- Do not introduce arbitrary new libraries without checking the ADRs.

# 2. Proactive Improvement
- If you notice a cleaner, more secure, faster, or modern architectural option:
  PROACTIVELY propose it to the user with pros/cons before proceeding.

# 3. Living Documentation
- When completing a task, check it off `[x]` in `docs/05-backlog/02-epics-and-tasks.md`.
- Keep schema/API changes synced with documentation in the same commit.
